{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The priests and he shall take a handful.</b> From the taking of the handful onward is the mitzvah of the priesthood (ibid.)." "<b>And he shall take a handful from there.</b> From the place where the feet of the non-priest stand; to teach you that the taking of the handful is valid anywhere in the courtyard, even within the eleven cubits that are the place treading by the feet of Israel (Yoma 16)." "<b>The full handful.</b> I might think overflow — spilling out to every side; Scripture says, in another place, ״וְהֵרִים מִמֶּנּוּ בְּקֻמְצוֹ״ (Leviticus 6) — nothing is valid except what is within the palmful. If בְּקֻמְצוֹ — I might think deficient; Scripture says מְלֹא. How so? He covers his three fingers over the flat of his palm — and this is a קֹמֶץ in the sense of the Hebrew language (Menachot 11)." "<b>Upon all its frankincense.</b> Apart from all the frankincense, the handful must be full." "<b>Its frankincense and he shall burn.</b> The frankincense too is included in the burning." "<b>The fill of his fist of its fine flour and of its oil.</b> So if he clenched and a grain of salt or a sliver of frankincense came up in his hand — it is disqualified (Menahot 6)." "<b>Its memorial portion.</b> The fistful that goes up on high — that is the memorial of the meal-offering: by it its owner is remembered for good and for contentment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:47.298492667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}